<https://repolex.ai/data/jmespath/jmespath.py/commit/45bd666bd446ab9b1b162e42081f0321959d04bd> <https://repolex.ai/ontology/extracts/gitpython-developers/GitPython/v3.1.46/core/message> "Initial commit that switches to an simpler AST\n\nThis commit is a pure refactoring, a non-functional change.\nThe internal have been restructured as follows:\n\n* The AST nodes have been switched to dictionaries instead of\n  classes.  In additional to getting pretty-printing for free now,\n  this also makes it the AST nodes purely data, the search() behavior\n  is now removed from AST nodes, effectively decoupling the AST\n  representation from the execution semantics of the AST nodes.\n* The search()'ing functionality has been extracted to an external\n  tree visitor.  The visitor interface also allows for a generic\n  mechanism for manipulating the AST in the future (i.e. AST\n  rewriting for optimization, emitting byte code).\n* The functions have been moved out to a separate module.  The\n  interpreter now takes a dependency on the runtime functions.\n  This also theoretically makes it possible for a user to add\n  new functions.\n\nThe only noticeable change from this change is that function\nname validation and arity validation are now at runtime instead\nof compile time.  By doing this though we now allow for user\nprovided functions." <https://repolex.ai/data/jmespath/jmespath.py/commit> .
