<https://repolex.ai/data/jmespath/jmespath.py/commit/565c480d5b4b1f471f1a375b90c38e406c01a787> <https://repolex.ai/ontology/extracts/gitpython-developers/GitPython/v3.1.46/core/message> "Perf improvement for parsing subexprs\n\nRather than having subexprs be a binary AST node,\nthe children key is now an array of N children.\nDuring parsing, if we encounter a subexpr, rather than\ncreating a new AST node, we just add to the children\nnode.\n\nThis not only improves parsing, but also improves search\ntime.\n\nFrom the perf tests, before:\n\nlex_time:      0.40006638\nparse_time:    0.70905685ms\nsearch_time:   0.11396408ms\ncombined_time: 0.83518028ms\nname: deep_nesting_50\n\nand after:\n\nlex_time:      0.40888786\nparse_time:    0.69713593ms\nsearch_time:   0.05698204ms\ncombined_time: 0.76007843ms\nname: deep_nesting_50" <https://repolex.ai/data/jmespath/jmespath.py/commit> .
